<article class="env-corollary" id="D4A82A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D4A82A">Corollary <span data-tag="D4A82A">5.2.2.4</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow S$ be a Cartesian fibration of simplicial sets. An edge $e: x \rightarrow y$ of $X$ is $p$-coCartesian if and only if it is locally $p$-coCartesian (see the discussion preceding Proposition <a href="/tag/3DFE8F" data-tag="3DFE8F">2.4.2.8</a>). </p>
